{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the `audit-log-archiver` CronJob, which looked like the cause, and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned 200. I haven't seen the grading result, so I don't know yet whether it passes.\n\n**What was wrong:** the archiver's `fluent-bit-sidecar` container never exited. Every Job therefore stayed Running with a pod stuck at `1/2 NotReady`. The CronJob's `Allow` policy started a new one every minute, so pods would have kept piling up in the namespace.\n\nThe application itself looked healthy when I checked. All its pods were running. Requests to the frontend's hotel search and recommendation endpoints returned 200 in a few milliseconds. I didn't find a fault in the app services, so the CronJob is a best guess at the cause, not a confirmed one.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Sidecar:** I moved it to a native sidecar, an init container with `restartPolicy: Always`, which Kubernetes 1.32 supports. Jobs now finish when the archiver finishes.\n- **Concurrency:** I set `concurrencyPolicy` to `Forbid`.\n- **Cleanup:** I deleted the two stuck Jobs.\n\nAfter the change, a new Job completed 1/1 in about 9 seconds."}}
